        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "b17ffbaa-58a5-39a8-82a2-aee378573019",
                "word": "bandoura",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "a532331a-0588-4c9e-89d8-7df3e921b92c",
                        "entry_id": "b17ffbaa-58a5-39a8-82a2-aee378573019",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "bandouras"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "5835c808-9d9a-4f6a-8999-31e138959b8a",
                        "entry_id": "b17ffbaa-58a5-39a8-82a2-aee378573019",
                        "tags": [],
                        "form": "bandura"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "75ca866d-f3e4-32f5-b748-c5b0ef2dbc85",
                        "entry_id": "b17ffbaa-58a5-39a8-82a2-aee378573019",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Instrument à cordes pincées de forme ovoïde, traditionnel en Ukraine, notamment chez les kobzari."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a8452469-a134-44f3-bc86-76d7b8a1ddc1",
                                "sense_id": "75ca866d-f3e4-32f5-b748-c5b0ef2dbc85",
                                "text": "L’ensemble formé de six jeunes femmes vêtues de costumes traditionnels chante en s’accompagnant d’un instrument ukrainien la bandoura, une petite harpe à 65 cordes."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "572cb5d8-f652-497b-8334-05f2e504fae2",
                                "sense_id": "75ca866d-f3e4-32f5-b748-c5b0ef2dbc85",
                                "text": "Symbole musical du peuple ukrainien, la bandoura à 65 cordes est un instrument fascinant. Aux XVe et XVIe siècles, la bandoura était l’instrument favori des Hetmans, les aristocrates ukrainiens."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4f2703c0-13f9-4eaa-84e8-2c2f7b283c76",
                                "sense_id": "75ca866d-f3e4-32f5-b748-c5b0ef2dbc85",
                                "text": "Parallèlement, l’institution du kobzar – le ménestrel ambulant familier, jouant de la bandoura, qui avait été autrefois un élément essentiel de la vie villageoise ukrainienne – disparut si brutalement que beaucoup crurent qu’ils avaient été arrêtés en masse."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "88285083-a393-48f2-b39c-907e3e6f47bb",
                                "sense_id": "75ca866d-f3e4-32f5-b748-c5b0ef2dbc85",
                                "text": "La bandoura à la main, se glissait loin des chanteurs le jeune Cosaque Levko, fils du bailli du village."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f842e32f-1826-4c91-b382-7e54485089f2",
                        "source_entry_id": "b17ffbaa-58a5-39a8-82a2-aee378573019",
                        "source_sense_id": "75ca866d-f3e4-32f5-b748-c5b0ef2dbc85",
                        "target_lang_word": "Bandura",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Bandura",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "636107d3-133e-3074-b92b-9dae7309ed7d",
                                        "entry_id": "a916da14-a8c9-329e-a313-e682d6b5b705",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "ukrainisches Saiteninstrument mit 12 bis 44 Saiten, das einer Laute ähnelt"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Musik"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b3580aba-d818-45b2-ab64-a96e72ebc464",
                                                "sense_id": "636107d3-133e-3074-b92b-9dae7309ed7d",
                                                "text": "Er spielt auf der Bandura."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d8bffc41-7ce0-4d15-93a8-6cdb86da9b6e",
                        "source_entry_id": "b17ffbaa-58a5-39a8-82a2-aee378573019",
                        "source_sense_id": "75ca866d-f3e4-32f5-b748-c5b0ef2dbc85",
                        "target_lang_word": "bandura",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "bandura",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a3248cef-21f7-317a-b883-33e95702d1cb",
                                        "entry_id": "41b28e1f-1a54-3ae4-8c10-91a084b61904",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A Ukrainian plucked stringed instrument with a tear-shaped body, like an asymmetrical lute or a vertical zither, which is played with both hands while held upright on the lap."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7daa5a70-afde-4448-b8e1-f751877d6d91",
                                                "sense_id": "a3248cef-21f7-317a-b883-33e95702d1cb",
                                                "text": "He touches the strings and pours forth a song descriptive of his live, his wanderings, his anguish, and is discovered by the magic tones of the bandura, his adventures, above all, by his voice and passionate fire."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c14c20f8-32ac-4a47-8d53-afda1407f7d6",
                                                "sense_id": "a3248cef-21f7-317a-b883-33e95702d1cb",
                                                "text": "The whole night passed amid shouts, songs, and rejoicings; and the rising moon gazed long at troops of musicians traversing the streets with bandouras, flutes, round balalaikas, and the church choir, who were kept in the Setch to sing in church and glorify the deeds of the Zaporozhtzi."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f64e1a24-9ea1-416a-a6e6-28eb781daf43",
                                                "sense_id": "a3248cef-21f7-317a-b883-33e95702d1cb",
                                                "text": "I have an old bandura hanging up on the wall in the hut. Opanás taught me to play on it, but there is no one to play it after me; and when I die, and that may be soon, perhaps nowhere in the wide world will one be found to play the bandura."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3c22790f-8857-44df-8bd0-1465b6d6274c",
                                                "sense_id": "a3248cef-21f7-317a-b883-33e95702d1cb",
                                                "text": "'Thank you, master, for your lesson. I will sing you a song if you will listen;' and he touched a string of the bandura."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "081c51e3-b94b-4260-ad86-22ba3cf31bae",
                                                "sense_id": "a3248cef-21f7-317a-b883-33e95702d1cb",
                                                "text": "It was only at this time that bandura players emerged from underground. They had been banned from playing under the Tsar, and then they emerged and began to remind everyone openly about their Cossack past and to awaken feelings of nationalism in young children."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2a18a709-8f43-4700-a190-000677395bcc",
                                                "sense_id": "a3248cef-21f7-317a-b883-33e95702d1cb",
                                                "text": "In the Ukraine of Russia the large bandoura with its almost circular face and as many as thirty strings (combining a zither function with fingered lute technique) is a popular short-necked lute, [...]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e091eeae-f8ca-40b2-84d4-78bb0aea715a",
                                                "sense_id": "a3248cef-21f7-317a-b883-33e95702d1cb",
                                                "text": "The bandura, a kind of zither, is unique to Ukraine and is considered the national instrument."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6c5de70e-501d-4dd8-8c01-839e31d7e804",
                                                "sense_id": "a3248cef-21f7-317a-b883-33e95702d1cb",
                                                "text": "The classical bandura is tuned diatonically and has 20 strings and wooden pegs; the Kharkiv bandura is tuned diatonically or chromatically and has a single string mechanism and 34 to 65 strings; and the Kyiv bandura, which has 55 to 64 strings, is tuned chromatically."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
